<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  datamodel="sce-static" (docs/SCE_ACCEPTED_SUBSET.md §2.15): one copy of a shared
  to-do list, for the world simulation (backends/rust/world). The same document is a
  person's copy and the hub the copies send to; `todo.join` says which.

  A to-do is a row of fields (todo_write): a title, whether it is done, a due day,
  whether it is removed. Each field of each to-do is a multi-value register: a write
  gives the field one more value, known by the stamp of the write (its dot), and a
  person who writes over a field writes over the values they have SEEN, no others. So
  two people who change the same field of one to-do at once, neither having seen the
  other's write, both keep theirs, on every copy, whatever order the changes reach it
  in and however many times each does; and a person who writes after seeing them
  replaces them all. A field with one value reads as that value, and with more than one
  says it was changed twice at once, and which values, for a person to choose from.

  The registers are an observed-remove set of the standard `orset_*` algorithms: a
  write is an add of the register's element with the write's dot as its tag, writing
  over a value is a tombstone of the value's tag, and what a field holds is the adds no
  tombstone names. A copy holds exactly those: a tombstone takes the add it names out of
  `adds` as it arrives (orset_live of the add and the tombstone), and an add that a
  tombstone already names is not taken in. So `adds` is the set's value, and a write is
  judged against the tombstones and the adds one pass each, never against every pair.
  The element is `id * 65536 + field`: a to-do is a uint32
  and a field a uint16 (todo_write), so the pair is one uint64 below 2^48 and no two
  registers share one, whatever the numbers; it is below 2^53 as well, which the
  Interpreter's integers hold exactly, so no lane meets a limit another does not.
  What a set cannot carry is the value itself, a number and a text, so each live add
  has its value in `values`, beside it, taken in when the add is live and taken out when a tombstone
  names it. The standard `mv_value_*` algorithms keep them: the machine assigns a
  write's text into a record of its own first (a payload's text is not handed to an
  algorithm, and that assignment is where a text past its bound is refused), and the
  record is what `mv_value_keep` records, bounded as its schema says, and
  `mv_value_drop` forgets. That is the whole of what this document adds to the merge.

  The clock is moved by what a copy sees as well as by what it does, as the sheet's
  is: a change made after reading someone else's sorts after it.

  A copy that has lost changes for good (restarted from an older save, so that what it
  lacks is something its peers believe delivered, and no retry repairs it) finds them with
  a digest and takes only what it lacks. Each copy keeps a merkle digest of its changes
  (merge/merkle_insert: a trie over the minute of each change's dot, a node the XOR of
  the hashes under it). A change is a live add or a tombstone; an add that a tombstone
  names leaves the digest when the tombstone arrives (XOR again), and the tombstone stays,
  so two copies hold the same digest exactly when they hold the same live adds and
  tombstones, whatever order the changes reached each in. The hash is a 32-bit mix of the
  register, the dot and whether it is an add or a tombstone (merge/merkle_change_hash),
  every part of each taken whole.

  The host raises `todo.resync` on a copy when its link is back. A message cannot carry a
  list, so the digest is not sent: it is walked, one node to a message (`todo.node`: depth,
  prefix, hash). A copy that is sent a node compares it with its own at that place; where
  they differ it answers with its own three children of the node (a child it holds
  nothing under is sent with hash 0, so the peer finds what only the peer holds), down to
  the last depth, 30, where a node is one minute: there each side sends the changes it
  holds for that minute as the ordinary `todo.write` and `todo.supersede` they were, which
  every copy takes in once whoever sends them and however often. merkle_diff is not used
  for the walk: it compares two whole digests held in one place, and here the peer's
  arrives a node at a time, so the walk is made by the messages. The digest's keeping is
  merkle_insert's.

  The root has three children and each node three, thirty levels down, which is every
  minute a signed 64-bit millisecond clock holds (merkle_node): a change at any wall time
  is on a path the walk takes. A wall time of today is under a run of fourteen nodes that
  hold the whole digest, which the walk passes one level to a message each; that is the
  same for every change however many there are, and a walk for many changes shares it.
  The messages of a walk are the nodes where the copies differ, three to a level, and
  grow with the changes they differ in and not with the time they were made at.

  A tombstone names its register by the element, and the supersede sent for it takes the
  element back to the to-do and the field (`element / 65536`, `element % 65536`).

  A copy that is written to for long enough has to forget what is settled, and the
  copies decide when they may. The host asks the hub (`todo.settle`: an instant); the hub
  asks each person's copy what it holds of the changes up to it (`todo.propose`); each
  person moves its clock past the instant, so that it stamps nothing at or before it
  again, and answers with a hash of its adds and tombstones up to it (`todo.ack`,
  event_settled). When both answers are the hub's own, every copy holds the same up to
  the instant and none will add to it, whatever order the messages came in and however
  often: the hub tells every copy to forget (`todo.floor`), and each forgets the
  tombstones it held when it answered. From then on a write
  stamped at or before the floor is not taken in: what a copy does not hold of it, it
  forgot. A copy whose answer was not the hub's, restarted from an old save, is told the
  floor and finds that it never held what the others settled: it forgets nothing and
  says it is `stale`, since the tombstones that would tell it which of its values were
  written over are gone from its peers. `todo.compact` is the host's own word, for a host
  that knows.

  A copy keeps every list in a room it is built with (`sce:limit`), and a write that
  would pass it fails half way, which no copy can undo. The host therefore gives a list less
  room than the build holds (`todo.room`), and a copy refuses a change of its own whole when it
  holds as much as it was given: before it stamps or sends anything, counted in `full`.
  What lifts it is a settle, which forgets tombstones. A change that is a person's own is the
  one judged, and what a person sent is taken in as it is, so the room is kept below the build's
  by what the people of one list can write at once.

  `values` and `digest` are what a run compares across copies.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml" xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       version="1.0" initial="open" datamodel="sce-static" name="todo_peer">
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_join.scxml" as="Join"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_edit.scxml" as="Edit"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_write.scxml" as="Write"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_supersede.scxml" as="Supersede"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_keep.scxml" as="Keep"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_node.scxml" as="PeerNode"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_visit.scxml" as="Visit"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_share.scxml" as="Share"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_agenda.scxml" as="Agenda"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="event_occurrence.scxml" as="Occurrence"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/merge/merkle_node.scxml" as="Node"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/merge/hlc_timestamp.scxml" as="Hlc"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/merge/orset_entry.scxml" as="Entry"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/merge/mv_value.scxml" as="Value"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/hlc_send.scxml" as="HlcSend"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/hlc_receive.scxml" as="HlcReceive"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/orset_union.scxml" as="OrsetUnion"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/orset_live.scxml" as="OrsetLive"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/mv_value_holds.scxml" as="MvValueHolds"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/mv_value_keep.scxml" as="MvValueKeep"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/mv_value_drop.scxml" as="MvValueDrop"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/merkle_insert.scxml" as="MerkleInsert"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/merkle_change_hash.scxml" as="MerkleChangeHash"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="event_schedule.scxml" as="Schedule"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="event_latest.scxml" as="EventLatest"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="event_conflict.scxml" as="EventConflict"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="event_agenda.scxml" as="EventAgenda"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_zone.scxml" as="Zone"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_compact.scxml" as="Compact"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/time/utc_from_local.scxml" as="UtcFromLocal"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_settle.scxml" as="Settle"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_propose.scxml" as="Propose"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_ack.scxml" as="Ack"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_floor.scxml" as="Floor"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="event_answer.scxml" as="Answer"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="event_settled.scxml" as="EventSettled"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_room.scxml" as="Room"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_role.scxml" as="Role"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="event_member.scxml" as="Member"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="event_roster.scxml" as="EventRoster"/>
  <datamodel>
    <data id="node" sce:type="uint64" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="hub" sce:type="bool" expr="false" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="clock" sce:type="record:Hlc" sce:direction="out">
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="stamp" sce:type="record:Hlc">
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <!-- The bounds of the lists a deployment may move are named (`sce:limit`): the
         lists of entries, of values and of the digest are as large as the standard
         algorithms that return them, which carry the same names, so a build that gives
         a name a number moves the machine and the algorithms together. -->
    <data id="adds" sce:type="list&lt;record:Entry&gt;" sce:capacity="1024" sce:limit="merge_entries" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="tombstones" sce:type="list&lt;record:Entry&gt;" sce:capacity="1024" sce:limit="merge_entries" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="one" sce:type="list&lt;record:Entry&gt;" sce:capacity="1024" sce:limit="merge_entries"/>
    <data id="stable" sce:type="list&lt;record:Entry&gt;" sce:capacity="1024" sce:limit="merge_entries"/>
    <data id="entry" sce:type="record:Entry">
      <sce:set name="element" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="values" sce:type="list&lt;record:Value&gt;" sce:capacity="512" sce:limit="merge_values" sce:direction="out"/>
    <!-- The text a person types, held to the 32 bytes a person writes (todo_edit): a write
         has room for more, for what a host puts there when it keeps the content from the hub
         (todo_write), and a text past 32 that a person typed is refused as one past the room. -->
    <data id="typed" sce:type="string" sce:capacity="32" expr="''"/>
    <data id="held" sce:type="record:Value">
      <sce:set name="id" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="field" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="value" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="text" expr="''"/>
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="digest" sce:type="list&lt;record:Node&gt;" sce:capacity="2048" sce:limit="merge_digest" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="mine" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="shareId" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="shareField" sce:type="uint16" expr="0"/>
    <data id="known" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="wasLive" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="isLive" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="present" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="refusals" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="agenda" sce:type="list&lt;record:Occurrence&gt;" sce:capacity="64" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="local" sce:type="list&lt;record:Occurrence&gt;" sce:capacity="64"/>
    <data id="occ" sce:type="record:Occurrence">
      <sce:set name="id" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="start" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="end" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nth" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="conflict" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="agendaNext" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <!-- The host's four time zones, a table of transitions each (todo.zone), and the
         table of the zone of the to-do the agenda is asked for. -->
    <data id="zoneStarts1" sce:type="list&lt;int64&gt;" sce:capacity="64"/>
    <data id="zoneOffsets1" sce:type="list&lt;int32&gt;" sce:capacity="64"/>
    <data id="zoneStarts2" sce:type="list&lt;int64&gt;" sce:capacity="64"/>
    <data id="zoneOffsets2" sce:type="list&lt;int32&gt;" sce:capacity="64"/>
    <data id="zoneStarts3" sce:type="list&lt;int64&gt;" sce:capacity="64"/>
    <data id="zoneOffsets3" sce:type="list&lt;int32&gt;" sce:capacity="64"/>
    <data id="zoneStarts4" sce:type="list&lt;int64&gt;" sce:capacity="64"/>
    <data id="zoneOffsets4" sce:type="list&lt;int32&gt;" sce:capacity="64"/>
    <data id="zoneStarts" sce:type="list&lt;int64&gt;" sce:capacity="64"/>
    <data id="zoneOffsets" sce:type="list&lt;int32&gt;" sce:capacity="64"/>
    <data id="zoneRows" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="split" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="sched" sce:type="record:Schedule">
      <sce:set name="zone" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="start" expr="-1"/>
      <sce:set name="length" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="freq" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="interval" expr="1"/>
      <sce:set name="days" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="count" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="until" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="bymonth" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="mdPos" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="mdNeg" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="invalid" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="op0" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="op1" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="op2" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="op3" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="op4" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="op5" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="op6" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="on0" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="on1" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="on2" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="on3" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="on4" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="on5" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="on6" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="spPos" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="spNeg" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="wkst" expr="1"/>
      <sce:set name="wnPos" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="wnNeg" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="yd0" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="yd1" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="yd2" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="yd3" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="yd4" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="yd5" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="ydn0" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="ydn1" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="ydn2" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="ydn3" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="ydn4" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="ydn5" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="gone" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="flag" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="rawCount" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="rawLast" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="utcSec" sce:type="int64" expr="0"/>
    <!-- What the copies have settled (todo.settle): `floor`, the instant up to which this
         copy has forgotten, `stale` when the hub settled an instant this copy did not
         hold the same of, and `late` the writes refused for being stamped at or before
         the floor. `frozenFor` and `frozenHash` are what the copy held of the tombstones
         and the adds up to the instant it was last asked about, kept in `stable`; the hub
         keeps the round it has open (`pending`, -1 for none) and what each person
         answered. -->
    <data id="floor" sce:type="int64" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="stale" sce:type="bool" expr="false" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="late" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="frozenFor" sce:type="int64" expr="-1"/>
    <data id="frozenHash" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="pending" sce:type="int64" expr="-1"/>
    <data id="members" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="agreeing" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="answers" sce:type="list&lt;record:Answer&gt;" sce:capacity="512"/>
    <data id="answer" sce:type="record:Answer">
      <sce:set name="sender" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="hash" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="agreed" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <!-- How much the host lets this copy hold (todo.room), 0 for no limit; the changes a
         person made that were refused for it (`full`); and what the change in hand is
         judged by: whether it is to a register that holds no value yet, and whether the
         copy is full. -->
    <data id="roomValues" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="roomHistory" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="roomDigest" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="full" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="fresh" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="blocked" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <!-- What the host lets each member do (todo.role), the changes that were refused for it
         (`denied`) and what the change in hand is judged by: whether its author may write. -->
    <data id="roster" sce:type="list&lt;record:Member&gt;" sce:capacity="64" sce:limit="todo_roster"/>
    <data id="denied" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="forbidden" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="authorized" sce:type="bool" expr="true"/>
  </datamodel>
  <state id="open">
    <transition event="todo.join" type="internal">
      <assign location="node" expr="_event.data.node"/>
      <assign location="hub" expr="_event.data.hub"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- What the host lets this copy hold (todo.room): the most values, tombstones and
         digest nodes. 0 is no limit of that kind. -->
    <transition event="todo.room" type="internal">
      <assign location="roomValues" expr="_event.data.values"/>
      <assign location="roomHistory" expr="_event.data.history"/>
      <assign location="roomDigest" expr="_event.data.digest"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- What the host lets a member do (todo.role): the member takes the role, or is taken
         off the roster by a role of 0. A copy with no roster refuses no one, and one with a
         roster refuses a change of its own member's that is not a writer's, and the hub
         what a member that is not a writer sends it. The roster is the host's word and the
         copies take it alike, as they take the room. -->
    <transition event="todo.role" type="internal">
      <assign location="roster" expr="EventRoster(roster, _event.data.node, _event.data.role)"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- A person's change: stamped, then handled as any write is, and sent to the hub.
         The values the person has seen in the field are the ones it writes over: each
         is named in a supersede, here and at the hub, before the write itself.

         A copy that holds as much as the host let it (todo.room) refuses the change
         whole, as it refuses a text that does not fit: before the clock moves and before
         anything is sent, so that no copy holds half of it, and counts it in `full` for
         the host to say that the list is full. A change to a register that already has
         a value adds none and is not refused for the values; a change when the tombstones
         or the digest are as many as allowed is, since each adds to them, and what lets it
         through is a settle. -->
    <transition event="todo.edit" type="internal">
      <!-- The text is read first, into a place nothing else reads: a text past its bound
           is an assignment that fails and ends the block, so the change is refused
           whole, with the clock where it was and nothing sent. The bound a person's text
           has is the one `typed` holds, and the one a write has is wider. -->
      <assign location="typed" expr="_event.data.text"/>
      <assign location="held.text" expr="_event.data.text"/>
      <assign location="entry.element" expr="_event.data.id"/>
      <assign location="entry.element" expr="entry.element * 65536 + _event.data.field"/>
      <assign location="fresh" expr="true"/>
      <foreach array="adds" item="o">
        <if cond="o.element === entry.element">
          <assign location="fresh" expr="false"/>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <!-- Whether the host let this copy's member write (todo.role): with no roster set,
           anyone; with one, a member whose role is a writer's. A change it may not make is
           refused as one that does not fit is, before the clock moves, and counted in
           `denied`. -->
      <assign location="forbidden" expr="false"/>
      <if cond="len(roster) &gt; 0">
        <assign location="forbidden" expr="true"/>
        <foreach array="roster" item="m">
          <if cond="m.node === node &amp;&amp; m.role &gt;= 2">
            <assign location="forbidden" expr="false"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
      </if>
      <assign location="blocked" expr="!forbidden &amp;&amp; ((roomValues &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; fresh &amp;&amp; len(values) &gt;= roomValues) || (roomHistory &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; len(tombstones) &gt;= roomHistory) || (roomDigest &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; len(digest) &gt;= roomDigest))"/>
      <if cond="forbidden">
        <assign location="denied" expr="denied + 1"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="blocked">
        <assign location="full" expr="full + 1"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="!blocked &amp;&amp; !forbidden">
        <assign location="clock" expr="HlcSend(clock, _event.data.now, node)"/>
        <foreach array="adds" item="o">
          <if cond="o.element === entry.element">
            <send target="#_internal" event="todo.supersede">
              <param name="id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
              <param name="field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
              <param name="wallTime" expr="o.wallTime"/>
              <param name="counter" expr="o.counter"/>
              <param name="nodeId" expr="o.nodeId"/>
              <param name="by" expr="node"/>
            </send>
            <send target="#server" event="todo.supersede">
              <param name="id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
              <param name="field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
              <param name="wallTime" expr="o.wallTime"/>
              <param name="counter" expr="o.counter"/>
              <param name="nodeId" expr="o.nodeId"/>
              <param name="by" expr="node"/>
            </send>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <send target="#_internal" event="todo.write">
          <param name="id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
          <param name="field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
          <param name="value" expr="_event.data.value"/>
          <param name="text" expr="_event.data.text"/>
          <param name="wallTime" expr="clock.wallTime"/>
          <param name="counter" expr="clock.counter"/>
          <param name="nodeId" expr="node"/>
        </send>
        <send target="#server" event="todo.write">
          <param name="id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
          <param name="field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
          <param name="value" expr="_event.data.value"/>
          <param name="text" expr="_event.data.text"/>
          <param name="wallTime" expr="clock.wallTime"/>
          <param name="counter" expr="clock.counter"/>
          <param name="nodeId" expr="node"/>
        </send>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A write stamped at or before the floor is not taken in, from anyone and however
         often it arrives. Everything up to the floor was settled when the copies agreed on
         it: a write of that time that this copy does not hold is one it forgot, with the
         tombstone that named it, and taking it in again would bring the value back. A
         person's copy stamps nothing at or before an instant it has answered for, so no
         write that is new is refused here. -->
    <transition event="todo.write" cond="floor &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; _event.data.wallTime &lt;= floor" type="internal">
      <!-- It is counted only when this copy does not hold it: a live write that a peer
           shows again, which a repair of another copy sends to every copy that reads the
           same name, is held and changes nothing. -->
      <assign location="held.id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
      <assign location="held.field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
      <assign location="held.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
      <assign location="held.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
      <assign location="held.nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
      <assign location="present" expr="MvValueHolds(values, held)"/>
      <if cond="!present">
        <assign location="late" expr="late + 1"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A write to a field, from a person here or from elsewhere: one more value, once.
         The hub takes it only from a member the host let write (todo.role): a write whose
         author is not on a roster that is set, or is on it with less than a writer's role,
         is dropped whole and counted in `denied`, as a change a person's copy was not let
         make is. -->
    <transition event="todo.write" type="internal">
      <assign location="authorized" expr="true"/>
      <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; len(roster) &gt; 0">
        <assign location="authorized" expr="false"/>
        <foreach array="roster" item="m">
          <if cond="m.node === _event.data.nodeId &amp;&amp; m.role &gt;= 2">
            <assign location="authorized" expr="true"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
      </if>
      <if cond="!authorized">
        <assign location="denied" expr="denied + 1"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="authorized">
        <!-- The same, for a write that arrives: one whose text does not fit changes
             nothing here and is passed on to no one, rather than being merged in part. -->
        <assign location="held.text" expr="_event.data.text"/>
        <if cond="_event.data.nodeId !== node">
          <assign location="stamp.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
          <assign location="stamp.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
          <assign location="stamp.nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
          <assign location="clock" expr="HlcReceive(clock, stamp, clock.wallTime, node)"/>
        </if>
        <!-- A write this copy made and no longer holds, which a peer sends back when the
             copy has been restarted from an older save, is taken in with the clock moved
             up to it, so that what the copy writes next is stamped after it and never with
             a dot it has already used. A write made here that the clock already stands at
             (every one, as it is first handled) moves nothing. -->
        <if cond="_event.data.nodeId === node &amp;&amp; (_event.data.wallTime &gt; clock.wallTime || (_event.data.wallTime === clock.wallTime &amp;&amp; _event.data.counter &gt; clock.counter))">
          <assign location="clock.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
          <assign location="clock.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
        </if>
        <assign location="entry.element" expr="_event.data.id"/>
        <assign location="entry.element" expr="entry.element * 65536 + _event.data.field"/>
        <assign location="entry.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="entry.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
        <assign location="entry.nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
        <!-- Whether the write is live: no tombstone names it. One a person wrote over
             before it arrived is not taken in, and only a live one is added. And whether
             its value is already held, which a write that arrives twice is. -->
        <assign location="isLive" expr="true"/>
        <foreach array="tombstones" item="t">
          <if cond="t.element === entry.element &amp;&amp; t.wallTime === entry.wallTime &amp;&amp; t.counter === entry.counter &amp;&amp; t.nodeId === entry.nodeId">
            <assign location="isLive" expr="false"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <if cond="isLive">
          <sce:clear target="one"/>
          <sce:append target="one" expr="entry"/>
          <assign location="adds" expr="OrsetUnion(adds, one)"/>
        </if>
        <assign location="held.id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
        <assign location="held.field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
        <assign location="held.value" expr="_event.data.value"/>
        <assign location="held.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="held.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
        <assign location="held.nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="present" expr="MvValueHolds(values, held)"/>
        <if cond="isLive &amp;&amp; !present">
          <assign location="values" expr="MvValueKeep(values, held)"/>
          <send target="#_internal" event="todo.keep">
            <param name="kind" expr="0"/>
            <param name="element" expr="entry.element"/>
            <param name="wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
            <param name="counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
            <param name="nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
          </send>
        </if>

        <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; _event.data.nodeId !== 1">
          <send target="#alice" event="todo.write">
            <param name="id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
            <param name="field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
            <param name="value" expr="_event.data.value"/>
            <param name="text" expr="_event.data.text"/>
            <param name="wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
            <param name="counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
            <param name="nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
          </send>
        </if>
        <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; _event.data.nodeId !== 2">
          <send target="#bob" event="todo.write">
            <param name="id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
            <param name="field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
            <param name="value" expr="_event.data.value"/>
            <param name="text" expr="_event.data.text"/>
            <param name="wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
            <param name="counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
            <param name="nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A value someone wrote over, from a person here or from elsewhere: its add is
         named by a tombstone, and its value, if held, is taken out. The hub takes it only
         from a member the host let write, as it takes a write (`by` is who wrote over). -->
    <transition event="todo.supersede" type="internal">
      <assign location="authorized" expr="true"/>
      <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; len(roster) &gt; 0">
        <assign location="authorized" expr="false"/>
        <foreach array="roster" item="m">
          <if cond="m.node === _event.data.by &amp;&amp; m.role &gt;= 2">
            <assign location="authorized" expr="true"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
      </if>
      <if cond="!authorized">
        <assign location="denied" expr="denied + 1"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="authorized">
        <assign location="entry.element" expr="_event.data.id"/>
        <assign location="entry.element" expr="entry.element * 65536 + _event.data.field"/>
        <assign location="entry.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="entry.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
        <assign location="entry.nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
        <!-- Whether the tombstone is new, which one that arrives twice is not. -->
        <assign location="known" expr="false"/>
        <foreach array="tombstones" item="t">
          <if cond="t.element === entry.element &amp;&amp; t.wallTime === entry.wallTime &amp;&amp; t.counter === entry.counter &amp;&amp; t.nodeId === entry.nodeId">
            <assign location="known" expr="true"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <sce:clear target="one"/>
        <sce:append target="one" expr="entry"/>
        <assign location="tombstones" expr="OrsetUnion(tombstones, one)"/>
        <!-- The add it names is no longer live: it leaves `adds` (a tombstone that is
             not new leaves nothing to take out). -->
        <assign location="adds" expr="OrsetLive(adds, one)"/>

        <!-- And whether the write it names is held, which is when its add leaves the
             digest as the tombstone enters it. -->
        <assign location="held.id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
        <assign location="held.field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
        <assign location="held.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="held.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
        <assign location="held.nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="wasLive" expr="MvValueHolds(values, held)"/>
        <assign location="values" expr="MvValueDrop(values, held)"/>
        <if cond="!known">
          <send target="#_internal" event="todo.keep">
            <param name="kind" expr="1"/>
            <param name="element" expr="entry.element"/>
            <param name="wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
            <param name="counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
            <param name="nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
          </send>
        </if>
        <if cond="wasLive">
          <send target="#_internal" event="todo.keep">
            <param name="kind" expr="0"/>
            <param name="element" expr="entry.element"/>
            <param name="wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
            <param name="counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
            <param name="nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
          </send>
        </if>

        <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; _event.data.by !== 1">
          <send target="#alice" event="todo.supersede">
            <param name="id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
            <param name="field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
            <param name="wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
            <param name="counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
            <param name="nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
            <param name="by" expr="_event.data.by"/>
          </send>
        </if>
        <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; _event.data.by !== 2">
          <send target="#bob" event="todo.supersede">
            <param name="id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
            <param name="field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
            <param name="wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
            <param name="counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
            <param name="nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
            <param name="by" expr="_event.data.by"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A change taken in for the first time, told to the digest: its hash is XORed
         into every node on the path of its minute. An add that a tombstone has named
         is told again, which takes it out. The hash is merkle_change_hash's, of the
         entry the change names and its kind. -->
    <transition event="todo.keep" type="internal">
      <assign location="entry.element" expr="_event.data.element"/>
      <assign location="entry.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
      <assign location="entry.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
      <assign location="entry.nodeId" expr="_event.data.nodeId"/>
      <assign location="mine" expr="MerkleChangeHash(entry, _event.data.kind)"/>
      <assign location="digest" expr="MerkleInsert(digest, _event.data.wallTime / 60000, mine)"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- The host's word that the changes up to an instant are settled everywhere: the
         tombstones stamped at or before it go, and leave the digest as they entered it
         (the same hash, XORed again), so that the digest is still the digest of what the
         copy holds, and a copy that is told the same instant holds the same. The adds
         they named left `adds` when each tombstone arrived, and a register's values are
         what no tombstone names, so neither is moved: the tombstones are what grows
         without it, and this is what lets a copy that is written to for years hold only
         what is current (orset_live, the difference that is how a set forgets). -->
    <transition event="todo.compact" type="internal">
      <sce:clear target="stable"/>
      <assign location="frozenFor" expr="-1"/>
      <foreach array="tombstones" item="t">
        <if cond="t.wallTime &lt;= _event.data.before">
          <sce:append target="stable" expr="t"/>
          <assign location="mine" expr="MerkleChangeHash(t, 1)"/>
          <assign location="digest" expr="MerkleInsert(digest, t.wallTime / 60000, mine)"/>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <assign location="tombstones" expr="OrsetLive(tombstones, stable)"/>
      <if cond="_event.data.before &gt; floor">
        <assign location="floor" expr="_event.data.before"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The host asks the hub to settle what is stamped at or before an instant, so that
         the copies decide the instant themselves and no host has to know that every copy
         holds everything up to it. The hub moves its clock past the instant, asks each
         person's copy what it holds (todo.propose), and repeats the last instant it
         settled to both, so that a copy that missed it is told again. -->
    <transition event="todo.settle" type="internal">
      <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; _event.data.before &gt; floor">
        <assign location="pending" expr="_event.data.before"/>
        <assign location="members" expr="_event.data.members"/>
        <sce:clear target="answers"/>
        <if cond="clock.wallTime &lt;= _event.data.before">
          <assign location="clock.wallTime" expr="_event.data.before + 1"/>
          <assign location="clock.counter" expr="0"/>
        </if>
        <send target="#alice" event="todo.propose">
          <param name="before" expr="_event.data.before"/>
        </send>
        <send target="#bob" event="todo.propose">
          <param name="before" expr="_event.data.before"/>
        </send>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A person's copy is asked what it holds up to an instant. It moves its clock past
         the instant first, so that what it stamps from now on is after it, and then
         takes what it holds of the tombstones up to the instant and the hash of the
         adds and tombstones (event_settled): the tombstones are what it will forget if
         the hub settles, and no others, so that a tombstone that arrives after it
         answered is kept with the value it names. -->
    <transition event="todo.propose" type="internal">
      <if cond="!hub &amp;&amp; _event.data.before &gt; floor">
        <if cond="clock.wallTime &lt;= _event.data.before">
          <assign location="clock.wallTime" expr="_event.data.before + 1"/>
          <assign location="clock.counter" expr="0"/>
        </if>
        <sce:clear target="stable"/>
        <foreach array="tombstones" item="t">
          <if cond="t.wallTime &lt;= _event.data.before">
            <sce:append target="stable" expr="t"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <assign location="frozenFor" expr="_event.data.before"/>
        <assign location="frozenHash" expr="EventSettled(adds, tombstones, _event.data.before)"/>
        <send target="#server" event="todo.ack">
          <param name="sender" expr="node"/>
          <param name="before" expr="_event.data.before"/>
          <param name="hash" expr="frozenHash"/>
        </send>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The hub reads an answer only for the round it has open, and keeps each distinct
         answer (a copy and the hash it gave). A copy whose answer is the hub's own,
         now, held exactly what the hub holds when it answered, and stamps nothing at or
         before the instant after: when as many different copies as the host named
         (`members`) have such an answer, every copy held the same up to the instant, and
         the instant is settled. The hub tells every copy, itself included, to forget. An
         answer that differs settles nothing; the round stays open for a later answer, or
         for the host's next todo.settle. -->
    <transition event="todo.ack" type="internal">
      <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; _event.data.before === pending">
        <assign location="mine" expr="EventSettled(adds, tombstones, pending)"/>
        <assign location="known" expr="false"/>
        <foreach array="answers" item="a">
          <if cond="a.sender === _event.data.sender &amp;&amp; a.hash === _event.data.hash">
            <assign location="known" expr="true"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <if cond="!known">
          <assign location="answer.sender" expr="_event.data.sender"/>
          <assign location="answer.hash" expr="_event.data.hash"/>
          <sce:append target="answers" expr="answer"/>
        </if>
        <!-- No copy has two answers of one hash, so the answers that are the hub's are
             as many as the copies that hold what it holds. -->
        <assign location="agreeing" expr="0"/>
        <foreach array="answers" item="a">
          <if cond="a.hash === mine">
            <assign location="agreeing" expr="agreeing + 1"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <if cond="members &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; agreeing &gt;= members">
          <sce:clear target="stable"/>
          <foreach array="tombstones" item="t">
            <if cond="t.wallTime &lt;= pending">
              <sce:append target="stable" expr="t"/>
            </if>
          </foreach>
          <assign location="frozenFor" expr="pending"/>
          <assign location="frozenHash" expr="mine"/>
          <send target="#alice" event="todo.floor">
            <param name="before" expr="pending"/>
            <param name="hash" expr="mine"/>
          </send>
          <send target="#bob" event="todo.floor">
            <param name="before" expr="pending"/>
            <param name="hash" expr="mine"/>
          </send>
          <send target="#_internal" event="todo.floor">
            <param name="before" expr="pending"/>
            <param name="hash" expr="mine"/>
          </send>
          <assign location="pending" expr="-1"/>
        </if>
        <!-- The copies are told the last instant settled when an answer is not the hub's
             and there was one: a copy that took part in it finds that it holds what was
             agreed or has forgotten it already, and one that did not (restarted from an
             old save) finds that it never did, and is stale. -->
        <if cond="_event.data.hash !== mine &amp;&amp; floor &gt; 0">
          <send target="#alice" event="todo.floor">
            <param name="before" expr="floor"/>
            <param name="hash" expr="agreed"/>
          </send>
          <send target="#bob" event="todo.floor">
            <param name="before" expr="floor"/>
            <param name="hash" expr="agreed"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The hub's word that an instant is settled. A copy that held what the hub says
         every copy held (it answered, or it holds it now) forgets the tombstones it held
         up to the instant, and stamps nothing at or before the
         instant from here on. A copy that holds another thing is not one the hub asked:
         it forgets nothing, and says it is stale, for the host to start it again from
         what its peers hold, since the tombstones its peers forgot are the ones that
         would tell it which of its values were written over. -->
    <transition event="todo.floor" type="internal">
      <if cond="_event.data.before &gt; floor">
        <if cond="frozenFor !== _event.data.before">
          <sce:clear target="stable"/>
          <foreach array="tombstones" item="t">
            <if cond="t.wallTime &lt;= _event.data.before">
              <sce:append target="stable" expr="t"/>
            </if>
          </foreach>
          <assign location="frozenFor" expr="_event.data.before"/>
          <assign location="frozenHash" expr="EventSettled(adds, tombstones, _event.data.before)"/>
        </if>
        <if cond="frozenHash === _event.data.hash">
          <if cond="clock.wallTime &lt;= _event.data.before">
            <assign location="clock.wallTime" expr="_event.data.before + 1"/>
            <assign location="clock.counter" expr="0"/>
          </if>
          <foreach array="stable" item="t">
            <assign location="mine" expr="MerkleChangeHash(t, 1)"/>
            <assign location="digest" expr="MerkleInsert(digest, t.wallTime / 60000, mine)"/>
          </foreach>
          <assign location="tombstones" expr="OrsetLive(tombstones, stable)"/>
          <assign location="floor" expr="_event.data.before"/>
          <assign location="agreed" expr="_event.data.hash"/>
          <assign location="stale" expr="false"/>
          <assign location="frozenFor" expr="-1"/>
        </if>
        <if cond="frozenHash !== _event.data.hash">
          <assign location="stale" expr="true"/>
        </if>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The host's word that this copy's link is back: it shows its peers the root of
         its digest. A person's copy has only the hub to show it to; the hub shows every
         person (to 0), however many the host has. -->
    <transition event="todo.resync" type="internal">
      <send target="#_internal" event="todo.visit">
        <param name="to" expr="0"/>
        <param name="depth" expr="0"/>
        <param name="prefix" expr="0"/>
        <param name="reply" expr="false"/>
      </send>
    </transition>

    <!-- Show a peer the node of this copy's digest at a place: the hash it holds there,
         0 where it holds nothing. -->
    <transition event="todo.visit" type="internal">
      <assign location="mine" expr="0"/>
      <foreach array="digest" item="n">
        <if cond="n.depth === _event.data.depth &amp;&amp; n.prefix === _event.data.prefix">
          <assign location="mine" expr="n.hash"/>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <if cond="!hub">
        <send target="#server" event="todo.node">
          <param name="sender" expr="node"/>
          <param name="to" expr="0"/>
          <param name="depth" expr="_event.data.depth"/>
          <param name="prefix" expr="_event.data.prefix"/>
          <param name="hash" expr="mine"/>
          <param name="reply" expr="_event.data.reply"/>
        </send>
      </if>
      <!-- The hub reaches its people by two names, `#alice` and `#bob`: the first is every
           person but the second and the second every person but the first, so that a
           person other than those two is reached by either, and the second only by its
           own. The node says whom it is for (`to`, 0 for all) and a person that it is
           not for lets it go. -->
      <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; _event.data.to !== 2">
        <send target="#alice" event="todo.node">
          <param name="sender" expr="node"/>
          <param name="to" expr="_event.data.to"/>
          <param name="depth" expr="_event.data.depth"/>
          <param name="prefix" expr="_event.data.prefix"/>
          <param name="hash" expr="mine"/>
          <param name="reply" expr="_event.data.reply"/>
        </send>
      </if>
      <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; (_event.data.to === 2 || _event.data.to === 0)">
        <send target="#bob" event="todo.node">
          <param name="sender" expr="node"/>
          <param name="to" expr="_event.data.to"/>
          <param name="depth" expr="_event.data.depth"/>
          <param name="prefix" expr="_event.data.prefix"/>
          <param name="hash" expr="mine"/>
          <param name="reply" expr="_event.data.reply"/>
        </send>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A node of a peer's digest: where this copy's own differs, the peer is shown the
         children of it, and at a minute the changes of that minute are sent. A node that
         is the same on both sides ends the walk there. At a minute the peer is also shown
         this copy's node once, so that it sends its changes too; that one is marked, and
         is not answered. -->
    <transition event="todo.node" type="internal">
      <if cond="hub || _event.data.to === 0 || _event.data.to === node">
        <assign location="mine" expr="0"/>
        <foreach array="digest" item="n">
          <if cond="n.depth === _event.data.depth &amp;&amp; n.prefix === _event.data.prefix">
            <assign location="mine" expr="n.hash"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <if cond="mine !== _event.data.hash &amp;&amp; _event.data.depth &lt; 30">
          <send target="#_internal" event="todo.visit">
            <param name="to" expr="_event.data.sender"/>
            <param name="depth" expr="_event.data.depth + 1"/>
            <param name="prefix" expr="_event.data.prefix * 3"/>
            <param name="reply" expr="false"/>
          </send>
          <send target="#_internal" event="todo.visit">
            <param name="to" expr="_event.data.sender"/>
            <param name="depth" expr="_event.data.depth + 1"/>
            <param name="prefix" expr="_event.data.prefix * 3 + 1"/>
            <param name="reply" expr="false"/>
          </send>
          <send target="#_internal" event="todo.visit">
            <param name="to" expr="_event.data.sender"/>
            <param name="depth" expr="_event.data.depth + 1"/>
            <param name="prefix" expr="_event.data.prefix * 3 + 2"/>
            <param name="reply" expr="false"/>
          </send>
        </if>
        <if cond="mine !== _event.data.hash &amp;&amp; _event.data.depth === 30">
          <send target="#_internal" event="todo.share">
            <param name="to" expr="_event.data.sender"/>
            <param name="minute" expr="_event.data.prefix"/>
          </send>
        </if>
        <if cond="mine !== _event.data.hash &amp;&amp; _event.data.depth === 30 &amp;&amp; !_event.data.reply">
          <send target="#_internal" event="todo.visit">
            <param name="to" expr="_event.data.sender"/>
            <param name="depth" expr="30"/>
            <param name="prefix" expr="_event.data.prefix"/>
            <param name="reply" expr="true"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The changes this copy holds that fall in one minute, sent to a peer as the
         writes and supersedes they were. A live write is held with its value; a
         tombstone names its register by the element, which is taken back to the
         to-do and the field. -->
    <transition event="todo.share" type="internal">
      <foreach array="values" item="v">
        <if cond="v.wallTime / 60000 === _event.data.minute">
          <assign location="shareId" expr="v.id"/>
          <assign location="shareField" expr="v.field"/>
          <if cond="!hub">
            <send target="#server" event="todo.write">
              <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
              <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
              <param name="value" expr="v.value"/>
              <param name="text" expr="v.text"/>
              <param name="wallTime" expr="v.wallTime"/>
              <param name="counter" expr="v.counter"/>
              <param name="nodeId" expr="v.nodeId"/>
            </send>
          </if>
          <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; _event.data.to !== 2">
            <send target="#alice" event="todo.write">
              <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
              <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
              <param name="value" expr="v.value"/>
              <param name="text" expr="v.text"/>
              <param name="wallTime" expr="v.wallTime"/>
              <param name="counter" expr="v.counter"/>
              <param name="nodeId" expr="v.nodeId"/>
            </send>
          </if>
          <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; _event.data.to === 2">
            <send target="#bob" event="todo.write">
              <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
              <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
              <param name="value" expr="v.value"/>
              <param name="text" expr="v.text"/>
              <param name="wallTime" expr="v.wallTime"/>
              <param name="counter" expr="v.counter"/>
              <param name="nodeId" expr="v.nodeId"/>
            </send>
          </if>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <foreach array="tombstones" item="t">
        <if cond="t.wallTime / 60000 === _event.data.minute">
          <assign location="shareId" expr="t.element / 65536"/>
          <assign location="shareField" expr="t.element % 65536"/>
          <if cond="!hub">
            <send target="#server" event="todo.supersede">
              <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
              <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
              <param name="wallTime" expr="t.wallTime"/>
              <param name="counter" expr="t.counter"/>
              <param name="nodeId" expr="t.nodeId"/>
              <param name="by" expr="node"/>
            </send>
          </if>
          <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; _event.data.to !== 2">
            <send target="#alice" event="todo.supersede">
              <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
              <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
              <param name="wallTime" expr="t.wallTime"/>
              <param name="counter" expr="t.counter"/>
              <param name="nodeId" expr="t.nodeId"/>
              <param name="by" expr="node"/>
            </send>
          </if>
          <if cond="hub &amp;&amp; _event.data.to === 2">
            <send target="#bob" event="todo.supersede">
              <param name="id" expr="shareId"/>
              <param name="field" expr="shareField"/>
              <param name="wallTime" expr="t.wallTime"/>
              <param name="counter" expr="t.counter"/>
              <param name="nodeId" expr="t.nodeId"/>
              <param name="by" expr="node"/>
            </send>
          </if>
        </if>
      </foreach>
    </transition>

    <!-- The host asks what a to-do has scheduled in a window: its occurrences there,
         read from the values the copy holds (event_agenda), for the host to show. Nothing
         is sent and nothing held changes; a to-do that has no schedule has no occurrences,
         and a window the scan cannot cover is a refusal that leaves the agenda empty. -->
    <transition event="todo.agenda" type="internal">
      <sce:clear target="agenda"/>
      <assign location="agendaNext" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="rawCount" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="rawLast" expr="0"/>

      <!-- The schedule of the to-do: each field it holds, as the value written last
           (event_latest), and whether two people changed one at once (event_conflict).
           The numbers are event_agenda's. -->
      <assign location="sched.zone" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 15, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.start" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 16, -1)"/>
      <assign location="sched.length" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 17, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.freq" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 18, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.interval" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 19, 1)"/>
      <assign location="sched.days" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 20, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.count" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 21, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.until" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 22, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.bymonth" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 23, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.mdPos" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 24, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.mdNeg" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 25, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.invalid" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 26, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.op0" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 45, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.op1" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 46, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.op2" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 47, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.op3" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 48, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.op4" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 49, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.op5" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 50, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.op6" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 51, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.on0" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 52, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.on1" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 53, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.on2" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 54, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.on3" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 55, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.on4" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 56, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.on5" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 57, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.on6" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 58, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.spPos" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 28, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.spNeg" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 29, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.wkst" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 30, 1)"/>
      <assign location="sched.wnPos" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 31, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.wnNeg" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 32, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.yd0" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 33, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.yd1" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 34, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.yd2" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 35, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.yd3" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 36, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.yd4" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 37, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.yd5" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 38, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.ydn0" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 39, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.ydn1" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 40, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.ydn2" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 41, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.ydn3" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 42, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.ydn4" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 43, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.ydn5" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 44, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.gone" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 9, 0)"/>
      <assign location="split" expr="EventConflict(values, _event.data.id)"/>
      <assign location="sched.flag" expr="0"/>
      <if cond="split">
        <assign location="sched.flag" expr="1"/>
      </if>

      <!-- That zone's table, as the one the conversion below reads. -->
      <sce:clear target="zoneStarts"/>
      <sce:clear target="zoneOffsets"/>
      <assign location="zoneRows" expr="0"/>
      <if cond="sched.zone === 1">
        <foreach array="zoneStarts1" item="s1"><sce:append target="zoneStarts" expr="s1"/><assign location="zoneRows" expr="zoneRows + 1"/></foreach>
        <foreach array="zoneOffsets1" item="o1"><sce:append target="zoneOffsets" expr="o1"/></foreach>
      </if>
      <if cond="sched.zone === 2">
        <foreach array="zoneStarts2" item="s2"><sce:append target="zoneStarts" expr="s2"/><assign location="zoneRows" expr="zoneRows + 1"/></foreach>
        <foreach array="zoneOffsets2" item="o2"><sce:append target="zoneOffsets" expr="o2"/></foreach>
      </if>
      <if cond="sched.zone === 3">
        <foreach array="zoneStarts3" item="s3"><sce:append target="zoneStarts" expr="s3"/><assign location="zoneRows" expr="zoneRows + 1"/></foreach>
        <foreach array="zoneOffsets3" item="o3"><sce:append target="zoneOffsets" expr="o3"/></foreach>
      </if>
      <if cond="sched.zone === 4">
        <foreach array="zoneStarts4" item="s4"><sce:append target="zoneStarts" expr="s4"/><assign location="zoneRows" expr="zoneRows + 1"/></foreach>
        <foreach array="zoneOffsets4" item="o4"><sce:append target="zoneOffsets" expr="o4"/></foreach>
      </if>

      <!-- With no zone the wall-clock readings are UTC instants. -->
      <if cond="zoneRows === 0">
        <assign location="agenda" expr="EventAgenda(sched, values, _event.data.id, _event.data.windowStart, _event.data.windowEnd, _event.data.skip)"/>
        <foreach array="agenda" item="a">
          <assign location="rawCount" expr="rawCount + 1"/>
          <assign location="rawLast" expr="a.nth"/>
        </foreach>
      </if>
      <!-- With one, the schedule is read in the zone's wall clock over the window widened
           by a day each side, which holds every reading an offset can bring into the
           window, and each occurrence is turned back into an instant by the table
           (utc_from_local: the first of an overlap, a gap read with the offset before it)
           and kept when it overlaps the window as asked. Its end is its start and its
           length, which a change of the clock does not change. -->
      <if cond="zoneRows !== 0">
        <assign location="local" expr="EventAgenda(sched, values, _event.data.id, _event.data.windowStart - 86400000, _event.data.windowEnd + 86400000, _event.data.skip)"/>
        <foreach array="local" item="l">
          <assign location="rawCount" expr="rawCount + 1"/>
          <assign location="rawLast" expr="l.nth"/>
          <assign location="occ.id" expr="l.id"/>
          <assign location="occ.nth" expr="l.nth"/>
          <assign location="occ.conflict" expr="l.conflict"/>
          <assign location="utcSec" expr="UtcFromLocal(zoneStarts, zoneOffsets, l.start / 1000)"/>
          <assign location="occ.start" expr="utcSec * 1000 + l.start % 1000"/>
          <assign location="occ.end" expr="occ.start + (l.end - l.start)"/>
          <if cond="(occ.end &gt; _event.data.windowStart || occ.start &gt;= _event.data.windowStart) &amp;&amp; occ.start &lt; _event.data.windowEnd">
            <sce:append target="agenda" expr="occ"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
      </if>

      <!-- A page that is full says where the next begins. -->
      <if cond="rawCount === 64">
        <assign location="agendaNext" expr="rawLast + 1"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The host's time zones, one transition at a time (a message cannot carry a list),
         in order of start, after todo.zone_clear. They are the host's and not shared: each
         copy reads the zones its own host tells it. -->
    <transition event="todo.zone" type="internal">
      <if cond="_event.data.zone === 1">
        <sce:append target="zoneStarts1" expr="_event.data.start"/>
        <sce:append target="zoneOffsets1" expr="_event.data.offset"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="_event.data.zone === 2">
        <sce:append target="zoneStarts2" expr="_event.data.start"/>
        <sce:append target="zoneOffsets2" expr="_event.data.offset"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="_event.data.zone === 3">
        <sce:append target="zoneStarts3" expr="_event.data.start"/>
        <sce:append target="zoneOffsets3" expr="_event.data.offset"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="_event.data.zone === 4">
        <sce:append target="zoneStarts4" expr="_event.data.start"/>
        <sce:append target="zoneOffsets4" expr="_event.data.offset"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <transition event="todo.zone_clear" type="internal">
      <sce:clear target="zoneStarts1"/>
      <sce:clear target="zoneOffsets1"/>
      <sce:clear target="zoneStarts2"/>
      <sce:clear target="zoneOffsets2"/>
      <sce:clear target="zoneStarts3"/>
      <sce:clear target="zoneOffsets3"/>
      <sce:clear target="zoneStarts4"/>
      <sce:clear target="zoneOffsets4"/>
    </transition>

    <transition event="error.execution" type="internal">
      <assign location="refusals" expr="refusals + 1"/>
    </transition>
  </state>
</scxml>
